  "heading": "\\axiom.of.extensionality",
  "heading_latex": "\\textrm{Axiom of Extensionality}",
  "body_text": null,
  "page": null,
  "source": "[\\axiom.of.extensionality]\nAxiom:\ngiven: X, Y is \\set\nwhere:\n. forAll: Z is \\set\n  then: (Z \"in\"? X) \\.iff./ (Z \"in\"? Y)\nthen: X = Y\nDocumented:\n. called: \"Axiom of Extensionality\"\n. description: \"Two sets are equal if and only if they have exactly the same\n                elements. The identity of a set is therefore nothing more than\n                the collection of its members, so any two constructions that\n                yield the same elements yield the same set.\"\nId: \"6fc3a89f-f8ef-420e-b1b6-6e5ed4905611\"",
